WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.556
Running the role offline, and reading it,

2
00:00:02.556 --> 00:00:06.200
shows what it leaves to you,
starting with owners and waves.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.213
It connects whatever the inventory
names, with no owner tags.

4
00:00:10.213 --> 00:00:14.888
It has no waves or batches, so one
mistake reaches everything at once.

5
00:00:14.888 --> 00:00:18.446
It can't do a real dry run on
a server without the agent;

6
00:00:18.446 --> 00:00:22.087
it wrongly decides the agent
is installed, then fails.

7
00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:24.996
Passing your own tags
silently drops its default

8
00:00:24.996 --> 00:00:27.975
that keeps database servers
from auto-onboarding.

9
00:00:27.975 --> 00:00:30.025
And it sends that signal by default.

10
00:00:30.025 --> 00:00:33.480
Each gap gets a fix, and
each is pinned by a test.
